## Scope
Implements OSM-FIX.2 source reconciliation without mutating ACTUAL or authorizing P9.1.

- keeps `data/sources/osm-current.json` as the cryptographically pinned ACTUAL OSM input;
- introduces `data/sources/osm-source-current.json` as the independently refreshable current OSM source;
- binds the exact 12 retired MD relations and one addition (21515245) in a fail-closed transition policy;
- requires authoritative HTTP 410 evidence for every retirement;
- records per-ID histories, versions, changesets, timestamps, CUATM context and SHA-256 evidence;
- treats 18967907 → 21515245 as an OSM cartographic-successor hypothesis only when same CUATM/change-set/timestamp evidence passes; legal succession remains UNRESOLVED;
- validates relation/way/node closure, source topology, snapshot hashes and historical/current geometry evidence;
- stages exact gzip snapshot bytes in the live artifact, fixing the incomplete artifact behavior observed after #397;
- moves freshness monitoring to the current-source manifest while leaving ACTUAL source-bundle fingerprint and release identity untouched;
- adds negative tests for unknown retirement, missing 410 evidence, unexpected addition metadata, and ACTUAL/source separation.

## Permanent guards
- `actual_mutation_allowed=false`
- `p91_import_allowed=false`
- `semantic_acceptance=BLOCKED_INCOMPLETE`
- no legal-parent or identity reassignment
- no relaxation of freshness thresholds or runner trust

The PR remains Draft until the live current-source candidate, per-ID evidence, exact snapshot bytes and all mandatory checks are verified.

## Acquisition update —21October2026

Previous verified head: `5a2a8870f4151aaa46815bcba2b444153e5067a7`; main85e9cdd reconciled without protected ACTUAL changes. Current-source acquisition now fetches unique pinned-epoch relation/way/node batches rather than re-expanding common geometry per relation. Exact per-ID scope, strict closure/topology, versions, SHA-256, 22-minute acquisition/one-hour restore boundaries and the14-day freshness threshold remain enforced. Only the current-source manifest selects this transport; the ACTUAL pin keeps its existing path.

148local Node tests PASS with real Python ZIP tests, no skips;32protected components/5848identities independently rechecked. Frozen evidence is verified against the Git index and staged blob SHA-256, including exact original logs in gzip. First CI on2ba11 rejected missing ignored plaintext evidence before any capture; that failed package and log are retained, and its outcome is not treated as a source/network result.

Exact-head CI is complete:19 workflows SUCCESS and1 FAILURE;29 check-runs SUCCESS and1 FAILURE. A/B, byte comparison, CodeQL and Chromium QA pass. Source run39684305238 failed at the RO inventory after two45-second timeouts (de and Kumi); its49 regression tests passed. No fresh RO inventory, complete RO/MD snapshot, source promotion or freshnessPASS exists. Supplemental bounded VKMaps and Geofabrik probes did not qualify an alternative provider. Draft/BLOCKED_SOURCE_TRANSITION remains mandatory. Proposed mapper operations are conditional boundary-way reference changes only:1376179876/v8 last index457,12318728194→12318728593;1376180731/v6 last index227,11649857778→8265822008. They preserve coordinates and target closure in simulation, while rejected alternatives would open five valid neighboring relations. Public editing is not authorized or performed; original-source review remains required.

See [technical comparison and conditional mapper dossier](https://github.com/ovidiudeica/reforma-teritoriala/blob/5a2a8870f4151aaa46815bcba2b444153e5067a7/docs/osm-fix2-layered-acquisition-20261021.md). PR remains Draft/BLOCKED_SOURCE_TRANSITION while upstream topology or any mandatory gate fails. Issue396 remains OPEN; P9.1 remains blocked.



